ha-citrine source patch 0002 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27): allowedEnergyTransfer in the
OCPP 2.1 AuthorizeResponse.

OCPP 2.1 added allowedEnergyTransfer to AuthorizeResponse: the energy transfer
modes the EV may choose for the session. When it is omitted the station SHALL
treat the session as charging only, so no session authorised by upstream
CitrineOS can be bidirectional. OCTT (OCA, Plugfest 23 October 2026) reported
the field missing; its CentralSetpoint TxProfiles were all Rejected.

The patch adds the lab's modes (DC, DC_BPT, AC_single_phase, AC_two_phase,
AC_three_phase, AC_BPT) to every Accepted OCPP 2.1 AuthorizeResponse that does
not set the field already. Other statuses and OCPP 2.0.1 (which has no such
field) are unchanged. Same behaviour as the compiled-JS patch of 0.7.5.

diff --git a/packages/ocpp/src/handlers/requests/2/authorize-request-ocpp-21-handler.ts b/packages/ocpp/src/handlers/requests/2/authorize-request-ocpp-21-handler.ts
index 4535d0e..8656703 100644
--- a/packages/ocpp/src/handlers/requests/2/authorize-request-ocpp-21-handler.ts
+++ b/packages/ocpp/src/handlers/requests/2/authorize-request-ocpp-21-handler.ts
@@ -364,6 +364,29 @@ export class AuthorizeRequestOcpp21Handler extends AbstractHandler {
     message: IMessage<OcppRequest>,
     response: OcppResponse,
   ): Promise<IMessageConfirmation> {
+    // ha-citrine patch (0002-ocpp21-allowed-energy-transfer): OCPP 2.1 treats an
+    // omitted allowedEnergyTransfer as charging only, so an Accepted session lists
+    // the lab's modes, bidirectional included.
+    const authorized = response as {
+      idTokenInfo?: { status?: unknown };
+      allowedEnergyTransfer?: string[];
+    };
+    if (
+      authorized.idTokenInfo?.status === AuthorizationStatusEnum.Accepted &&
+      !authorized.allowedEnergyTransfer
+    ) {
+      response = {
+        ...response,
+        allowedEnergyTransfer: [
+          'DC',
+          'DC_BPT',
+          'AC_single_phase',
+          'AC_two_phase',
+          'AC_three_phase',
+          'AC_BPT',
+        ],
+      } as OcppResponse;
+    }
     const status =
       (response as { idTokenInfo?: { status?: unknown } }).idTokenInfo?.status ??
       (response as { idTagInfo?: { status?: unknown } }).idTagInfo?.status;
